  "equipment_type": "Sensor (dew point transmitter)",
  "applies_to": "DMT143 dew point transmitters ordered with the Modbus RTU option (user guide M211435EN-L).",
  "summary": "The DMT143 is a compact Vaisala DRYCAP dew point transmitter for compressed air and dryers. Units with the Modbus option are Modbus RTU slaves on RS-485. This map covers dew/frost point and ppm readings, pressure compensation, filtering, serial settings, the LED alarm and test registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 240,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 2,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "The guide numbers registers in decimal starting at 1 and also prints the 0-based hex address used in the request; register number 1 is address 0x0000 on the wire."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "DMT143 User Guide",
    "doc_number": "M211435EN-L",
    "revision_date": "2026-01",
    "url": "https://docs.vaisala.com/r/M211435EN-L/en-US",
    "pages": "Appendix A Modbus reference, pp. 94-102 (Tables 31-40)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All registers are holding registers: read with function 03, write with function 16.",
    "32-bit floats put the least significant word at the listed register (CDAB). The guide states this and its worked read example confirms it.",
    "Unavailable data reads as quiet NaN (float) or 0x8000 (16-bit integer) rather than an exception.",
    "Integer dew point registers are value x 100 (raw x 0.01).",
    "Left out: the error code register. The guide prints it as number 515 with address 0x0203, which do not match (515 would be 0x0202), so the correct address is not clear.",
    "Pressure registers 769 and 771 are in bar (absolute), not hPa."
  ],
